usbands burning brides whose dowries have been spent; men appropriating women&#x2019;s earnings and widows&#x2019; land; banks discriminating against women applying for loans; corporations paying women less than men; men treating women as their intellectual inferiors due to primitive notions of female brain development; governments depriving women of affordable childcare; and so much more. As Scott takes us from the streets of Accra, where sex trafficking is widespread, to American business schools, where women are routinely patronized, the pervasiveness of the Double X Economy becomes glaringly obvious. But Scott believes that this rampant problem can be solved.","publicationYear":2020,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Women","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Economic conditions","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Feminist economics","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Women in economic development","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"BUSINESS & ECONOMICS / Women in Business","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"POLITICAL SCIENCE / Public Policy / Economic Policy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-double-x-economy-linda-scott"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Women's Studie